      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Prostitution is legal in the Netherlands: the Sex Work Act (2000) allows consenting adults to sell sexual services under licensing and health‑safety regulations.",
      "evidence": "Dutch government publications and the Sex Work Act (Wet regulering prostitutie) state that prostitution is a lawful profession when operated in licensed venues.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Euthanasia is legal in the Netherlands when strict medical criteria are met, as set out in the Termination of Life on Request and Assisted Suicide Act (2002).",
      "evidence": "The Act permits physicians to perform euthanasia without criminal liability if due‑care criteria are satisfied; court‑review procedures confirm legality.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Cannabis (and other soft drugs) is not \"totally legal\": possession of up to 5 g is a misdemeanor (gedoogbeleid) and sale is only tolerated in licensed coffee‑shops; the Opium Act still classifies cannabis as an illegal substance.",
      "evidence": "Dutch Opium Act lists cannabis as a controlled substance; policy of tolerance (gedoogbeleid) means authorities refrain from prosecution within limits, but the activity remains illegal on paper.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Hard drugs (e.g., heroin, cocaine) remain illegal and are criminal offences under the Opium Act.",
      "evidence": "The Opium Act distinguishes between soft and hard drugs; hard drugs are prohibited with criminal penalties for possession and trafficking.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Option C states that prostitution and euthanasia are legal (with some restrictions) and does not claim any drugs are legal.",
      "evidence": "Option C wording matches the facts established in steps 2 and 3 and avoids the false claim about drugs.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "depends_on": [2, 3]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "claim": "All other options (A, B, D, E, F) assert that cannabis, soft drugs, or drugs in general are legal, which contradicts step 4 (and step 5).",
      "evidence": "Steps 4 and 5 show that no drug category is \"totally legal\" in the strict sense.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [4, 5]
    },
